# OpenCPN External Control Demo — @PLATFORM@

This isolated developer package demonstrates the authenticated OpenCPN
`/api/v2` external-control architecture with xGRIB, xWeatherRouting and the
human-readable Scheduler. It targets `@EXPECTED_UNAME@` systems running
Debian 12 or a compatible Raspberry Pi OS 64-bit release.

It is a developer demonstration, not a navigation release. It does not replace
an existing OpenCPN installation, use an existing profile, activate routes or
send autopilot output. Chart, credential and forecast data are not included.

Install the target-distribution runtime prerequisites first. For Debian 12:

```sh
sudo apt-get update
sudo apt-get install curl file iproute2 libaec0 libblosc1 libeccodes0 \
  libhdf5-103-1 libhdf5-hl-100 libnetcdf19 libproj25 libqhull-r8.0 \
  libsz2 libzip4 python3-tk python3-venv
```

The demo installer itself uses no `sudo`; these are normal host runtime
packages used by OpenCPN and the bundled environmental-data helper.

Install into a new directory:

```sh
sha256sum --check ../OpenCPN-External-Control-Demo-*.tar.gz.sha256
./install-external-control-demo.sh "$PWD/Test-OpenCPN-External-Control-Demo"
Test-OpenCPN-External-Control-Demo/bin/launch-opencpn-external-control-demo
```

The installer checks the CPU architecture and every embedded checksum before
extracting. It stages the complete installation, reports missing shared
libraries, refuses to overwrite a non-empty target and generates a fresh
owner-only least-privilege token.

On first start, add only test charts you are entitled to use, disable the
bundled GRIB and original Weather Routing plug-ins, then enable xGRIB and
xWeatherRouting. Close OpenCPN cleanly before first launching the Scheduler:

```sh
Test-OpenCPN-External-Control-Demo/bin/launch-opencpn-scheduler-external-control-demo
```

Please report the package platform, Raspberry Pi model or computer, operating
system, wxWidgets version, the redacted OpenCPN log and the exact workflow
which failed. Never publish API tokens, provider passwords or licensed charts.
